From 01230a34c26a2a0ef98cc8d0b608a7f875f2e3c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Mendez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:33:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vendor: unix: set R12 before the ppc64x syscall branch

The four ppc64x syscall trampolines jump to the global entry point of
the generated ABI0 wrapper without setting R12. In a PIE that entry
point derives its TOC from R12, as ELFv2 requires of a caller entering
there, so the callee computes a wrong TOC and every global access
afterwards reads or writes the wrong memory. Any PIE binary that calls
unix.Syscall dies at startup on ppc64le.

Loading the target address into R12 instead of R31 fixes it and keeps
the indirect jump, so this does not reintroduce the linker range
problem that golang/go#81981 reported. In a non-PIE build the wrapper
has no TOC prologue and never reads R12, so nothing changes there.

Measured on a ten line program that calls unix.Syscall once, cross
compiled for ppc64le and run under qemu-user, three runs each:

    unpatched  -buildmode=pie     SIGSEGV  3/3
    patched    -buildmode=pie     ok       3/3
    unpatched  no -buildmode=pie  ok       3/3

Debian's ppc64el buildd hit this on real hardware while building siso,
which is how it was found.

Fixes golang/go#82324

Backport of golang.org/x/sys commit f5cb0306ac (https://go.dev/cl/850585),
fixing PIE binaries crashing at startup on ppc64le with x/sys v0.49.0.
See golang/go#82324 and lxc/incus#4301.
---
 vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/asm_linux_ppc64x.s | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/asm_linux_ppc64x.s b/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/asm_linux_ppc64x.s
index 2e1f4c3..daa8571 100644
--- a/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/asm_linux_ppc64x.s
+++ b/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/asm_linux_ppc64x.s
@@ -14,13 +14,13 @@
 // The runtime may know about them.
 
 TEXT ·Syscall(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-56
-	MOVD	$syscall·Syscall(SB), R31
-	MOVD	R31, CTR
+	MOVD	$syscall·Syscall(SB), R12
+	MOVD	R12, CTR
 	JMP	(CTR)
 
 TEXT ·Syscall6(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-80
-	MOVD	$syscall·Syscall6(SB), R31
-	MOVD	R31, CTR
+	MOVD	$syscall·Syscall6(SB), R12
+	MOVD	R12, CTR
 	JMP	(CTR)
 
 TEXT ·SyscallNoError(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-48
@@ -39,13 +39,13 @@ TEXT ·SyscallNoError(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-48
 	RET
 
 TEXT ·RawSyscall(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-56
-	MOVD	$syscall·RawSyscall(SB), R31
-	MOVD	R31, CTR
+	MOVD	$syscall·RawSyscall(SB), R12
+	MOVD	R12, CTR
 	JMP	(CTR)
 
 TEXT ·RawSyscall6(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-80
-	MOVD	$syscall·RawSyscall6(SB), R31
-	MOVD	R31, CTR
+	MOVD	$syscall·RawSyscall6(SB), R12
+	MOVD	R12, CTR
 	JMP	(CTR)
 
 TEXT ·RawSyscallNoError(SB),NOSPLIT,$0-48
